{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And the children of Israel walked, etc.</b> The reason this matter was stated a second time is perhaps that it intends to say that the Egyptians knew this thing — that Israel passed through on the dry land and the waters were a wall for them, etc., while they [the Egyptians] descended beneath the earth, and through this they knew HaShem, as He blessed be He said (Exodus 14:18): ״וְיָדְעוּ מִצְרַיִם״ etc.; without this they would not have perceived the matter. And go out and learn (Ibn Ezra on Exodus 14:27) from the fact that certain fools erred and said that Moses knew the hours at which the sea would subside, etc., and he brought Israel across at that time while the Egyptians did not know and drowned. This wonder removes the madness of that notion, for they walked on dry land and the waters were a wall — these two signs uproot the denial of the miracle, and HaShem showed them to the drowned ones."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:28:09.164468509Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}